{
  "raw": {
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001223978206": {
      "title": "Residential Life Coordinator",
      "description": "Residential Life Coordinator. Residential Life Coordinator Maryville University | St. Louis, Missouri Maryville University is seeking a Residential Life Coordinator to help lead and shape our on-campus living communities. In this position, you will support student growth through engaging programming, meaningful connections, and everyday leadership. From mentoring student staff to managing the operations of a vibrant residential community, you will play a central role in creating a place where students feel at home and supported. What You'll Do Leadership and Supervision Select, train, supervise, mentor, and evaluate a Graduate Assistant and Resident Assistants within your assigned area. Manage residential areas consisting of 150–550 residents. Work with Coordinators, the Graduate Assistant, and the Director of Residential Life to create department goals, training and development, learning outcomes, and assessment plans aligned with the University's vision and strategic plan. Program Development, Implementation, and Assessment Lead and support student programming efforts and assist with program advisement, implementation, marketing strategy, training, and coverage. Advise, promote, and attend programs for the Housing Experience (HEX) Programming Board. Manage Resident Assistant programming to ensure it reflects departmental values, aligns with Student Affairs wellness initiatives, and meets the needs of the diverse population of residential students. Collect program evaluations and attendance data, track engagement in residential spaces, and achieve strategic goals in line with the University mission. Execute large-scale campus-wide traditions in partnership with the Center for Student Engagement & Belonging, Athletics, and other campus partners. Professional Staff On-Call Participate in on-call responsibilities, crisis intervention, and conflict resolution. Assist in contacting/requesting emergency transportation of residential students to health care facilities. Collective Partnerships Work closely with the Center for Student Engagement and Belonging, Athletics, Admissions, and other campus partners on campus-wide initiatives. Serve on a variety of committees within the Division of Student Affairs and University community. Student Conduct Enforce University policies and procedures as a conduct hearing officer for designated spaces. Collaborate with the Dean of Campus Life on reviewing cases that may involve student bias or Title IX incident reporting. Serve as a Residential Life reviewer and liaison for conduct adjudication, consulting regularly with the Director of Residential Life. Recruitment and Retention Support residential students and families with excellent customer service. Contribute to enrollment goals by designing programs that support recruitment and retention. Participate in New Student Orientation, Admissions visit days, University Scholars Weekend, and other university-wide events. Assist with planning and executing campus-wide programs, including orientation and student on-boarding, in collaboration with campus partners. Building Management Oversee opening and closing of residential facilities during University recesses and supervise check-in/check-out operations. Coordinate room changes and placements in conjunction with the Director of Residential Life. Maintain residential hall records and inventories; manage key issuance/replacement and damage assessment/billing. Partner with Facilities staff regarding maintenance issues and building work orders. Other Maintain a high profile and visibility at student programs, athletic events, and campus initiatives, which may include evenings, weekends, holidays, and times when classes are not in session. Attend Student Affairs meetings, trainings, retreats, and planning sessions as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. What We're Looking For Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree in student development or a related field preferred. Knowledge of Student Development Theory. High competency in using technology for program and building operations. Exemplary skills in program development and implementation. Strong commitment to ethnic and cultural diversity. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Supervision experience. Current driver's license and ability to obtain certification to drive University vans. Ability to lift and carry up to 40 pounds. Preferred Skills A minimum of 2 years of experience working in a college or university setting, preferably Residential Life. Experience with event management software, housing software, and conduct software. Experience implementing restorative conduct methods to repair and restore communities. Certification in Mental Health First Aid. Familiarity with trauma-informed response techniques and ability to apply these practices when supporting students in crisis. Unusual Working Conditions, if any: This is a 12 month, professional live in position with on-call responsibilities. Flexibility in scheduling, including evenings, weekends, and holidays, based on student and institutional needs, is also required. Basic meal plan is provided to support interaction and community building with students in the dining hall. Why Maryville? As the Residential Life Coordinator, you will shape the residential experience for communities of students, mentor the next generation of student leaders, and help build communities where students feel at home. You'll collaborate with partners across campus—from Athletics to the Center for Student Engagement and Belonging—and contribute to a campus culture grounded in care and belonging. Join a university community committed to helping students learn deeply, serve boldly, and lead with heart. Compensation & Benefits : Salary Range: $35,000 - $40,000 annually Actual compensation will be commensurate with education, experience, skills, internal equity, and market considerations. Benefits unique to this position: Since this is an on-site position, you will receive free room, board and meal plan benefits in edition to your base salary Benefits Highlights : Maryville University offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support the health, financial well-being, and professional growth of our employees. Eligible employees enjoy access to: Medical, dental, and vision coverage Retirement plan with 100% University matching up to 9% contributions University-paid life and long-term disability insurance Generous paid time off, including 18 holidays, 3 weeks of vacation, 12 sick days, and 4 personal days Full/Partial Tuition waived for employees and eligible dependents Hybrid and flexible work schedules Wellness programs and employee assistance resources Free parking, fitness center access, and other campus perks"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001223382206": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Registration and Graduation Operations",
      "description": "Associate Director of Registration and Graduation Operations. Overall Job Summary: To collaborate with the Senior Director and Director of Academic Records and provide guidance and support to the Registration and Graduation Operations team. Supervisor Responsibilities: Supervises Academic Record Specialists, Veterans Services Coordinator, and Enrollment Operation Specialists. Essential Responsibilities: Provide direction and support to the Registration and Graduation Operations team. Serve as an escalation point for matters including registration, grades, class schedule, and graduation. Collaborate with departments across the university to provide clarity and support regarding Academic Records processes. Conduct training sessions for staff to enhance their understanding of policies and procedures. Maintain and manage the integrity of academic records, ensuring compliance with relevant policies and regulations as it relates to Petition for Exception to Policy, graduation, grade changes, and personal information updates. Provide support to students, faculty, and staff regarding academic records inquiries. Monitor and ensure the accuracy of student and academic data in the records system. Conduct regular data analysis to identify trends, discrepancies, and areas for improvement. Represent Strategic Enrollment Management in the Commencement Workgroup and provide data for commencement, communication with graduates, and volunteer for the event. Represent Registration and Graduation Operations on the Petition for Exception to Policy committee. Perform other daily and annual duties related to case resolution, process functions, knowledge article reviews, reporting, and quality assurance to accurate data. Qualifications: Several years of experience in academic records management or a related area. Familiarity with relevant regulations, policies, and best practices. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively and lead a team. Proficiency in relevant software and databases. Required Education: Master's degree in a related field (e.g., Higher Education Administration, Information Management). Compensation & Benefits Salary Range: $54,531 - $70,000 annually Actual compensation will be commensurate with education, experience, skills, internal equity, and market considerations. Benefits Highlights Maryville University offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support the health, financial well-being, and professional growth of our employees. Eligible employees enjoy access to: Medical, dental, and vision coverage Retirement plan with 100% University matching up to 9% contributions University-paid life and long-term disability insurance Generous paid time off, including 18 holidays, 3 weeks of vacation, 12 sick days, and 4 personal days Full/Partial Tuition waived for employees and eligible dependents Hybrid and flexible work schedules Wellness programs and employee assistance resources Free parking, fitness center access, and other campus perks"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001220889906": {
      "title": "Director of Clinical Education",
      "description": "Director of Clinical Education. Essential Responsibilities : What You Will Be Doing The Director of Clinical Education’s primary responsibilities during this 11-month appointment are to plan, coordinate, facilitate, administer, and monitor activities on behalf of the academic program and in coordination with academic and clinical faculty. This includes: Communication between Maryville University and the Affiliated Clinical Education Sites Clinical Education Program Planning, Implementation, and Assessment Clinical Site and Clinical Faculty Development Preparation of students for clinical experiences and advising students on clinical selection Evaluation of student performance in cooperation with the program director, other faculty, and the clinical instructor The Director of Clinical Education oversees all activities related to clinical experiences. This includes: Ensuring all Students are ready to enter clinical experiences and have the opportunity for success which includes: Review all clinical experiences evaluations by the students and clinical instructors to facilitate change in the clinical experience if needed. Oversee and review all clinical site visits scheduling of faculty and review of documentation post-visit to ensure success of the students. Presenting all students and their clinical placements to the faculty for review to ensure students have met the following 4 areas to move into clinical experiences. Safety Professional Behavior Communication Knowledge Monitoring and tracking all students' progress through clinical experiences. Manages the business of clinical education . Present to faculty CPI Results (Overall and Individual Student) and any comments/issues by clinical instructors that may need to be addressed by the program. Update the clinical handbook annually and ensure students and clinical sites are aware of any updates. Utilize the EXXAT system for clinical updates and site/student matching process. Meet deadlines for: Maryville University Legal Team (contracts and issues related to NC-SARA) EXXAT for clinic matching All reports needed for CAPTE, HLC, and any other university requirements. Clinical Management - The DCE is responsible to ensure: All clinical sites are updated and current. On March 1st each year a request for clinical slots the following year is sent. Establishment of agreements with clinical experience sites and ensures all clinical site agreements are current. Ensure all clinical instructors meet requirements and are qualified to be a clinical instructor. Ensure all clinical instructors are trained in the use of the CPI. All students are submitted into the system going into the 5th year and matched to sites according to the established timeline; current 6th year students are matched for their three terminal clinical experiences in early fall. Then, 5th year students are matched for their first integrated clinical experience. All communication with clinical sites is updated and current. All documentation for each clinical experience is up to date and provided with clinical sites with letters regarding student placement. Required Qualifications : To perform this job satisfactorily, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability, and environmental conditions required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Required Knowledge : Must be PT-licensed (or eligible for license) in the State of Missouri. Required Skills and Abilities : Experience in clinical education as a clinical instructor, site coordinator, previous DCE experience, and have completed 3.0 CPI Training. Required Formal Education : Advanced Academic Degree or Doctor of Physical Therapy Degree Required. Certifications Preferred. The above statements describe the job's essential responsibilities and requirements. They are not an exhaustive list of the duties that may be assigned to job incumbents. Compensation & Benefits : Salary Range: $85,000 - $112,000 annually Actual compensation will be commensurate with education, experience, skills, internal equity, and market considerations. Benefits Highlights : Maryville University offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support the health, financial well-being, and professional growth of our employees. Eligible employees enjoy access to: Medical, dental, and vision coverage Retirement plan with 100% University matching up to 9% contributions University-paid life and long-term disability insurance Full/Partial Tuition waived for employees and eligible dependents Hybrid and flexible work schedules Wellness programs and employee assistance resources Free parking, fitness center access, and other campus perks"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001215011606": {
      "title": "Admissions Representative",
      "description": "Admissions Representative. At Maryville University, we believe every student has a story, a purpose, and unlimited potential. As an Admissions Representative , you'll play a pivotal role in helping prospective students discover where their journey begins. Through relationship-building, strategic territory management, and personalized guidance, you'll serve as a trusted advisor from a student's first interaction with Maryville through enrollment. If you're energized by connecting with people, traveling, achieving goals, and making a meaningful impact, we'd love to meet you. What You'll Do As an Admissions Representative, you'll manage an assigned recruitment territory while serving as the primary enrollment advisor for prospective students throughout the admissions process. Territory Management & Recruitment Strategy Manage an assigned recruitment territory and develop strategic annual recruitment plans aligned with university enrollment goals. Build and maintain strong relationships with high schools, counselors, community organizations, and educational partners. Analyze territory demographics, enrollment trends, and market data to identify opportunities for growth. Monitor territory performance and adjust recruitment strategies using data and market intelligence. Meet or exceed territory enrollment goals while contributing insights to strengthen university-wide recruitment efforts. Student Recruitment & Enrollment Counseling Serve as the primary admissions counselor for prospective students from inquiry through enrollment. Build meaningful relationships through personalized outreach, advising, and ongoing communication. Conduct admissions appointments in person, virtually, and by phone. Guide students and families through every stage of the enrollment process, including: Application completion Transcript submission Financial aid Admission acceptance Enrollment deposit Registration Orientation Final enrollment Help students explore academic programs, scholarships, campus life, student services, and the overall Maryville experience. Enrollment Conversion & CRM Management Manage assigned applicant and admitted student populations using the University's CRM. Execute strategic outreach plans to improve application completion, deposits, and enrollment. Utilize enrollment dashboards, predictive analytics, and engagement data to prioritize outreach. Maintain accurate and timely documentation of all student interactions. Support enrollment marketing initiatives and yield campaigns that strengthen enrollment outcomes. Recruitment Events & Campus Engagement Represent Maryville University at high schools, college fairs, community events, transfer events, and other recruitment activities. Support individual visits, open houses, admitted student events, yield programs, and virtual recruitment events. Deliver engaging presentations to students, families, counselors, and community partners. Assist in planning and executing recruitment events that create exceptional prospective student experiences. Collaboration & Student Success Partner closely with Financial Aid, Student Financial Services, Marketing & Communications, Student Success, Academic Colleges, Athletics, Student Records, International Recruitment, and other campus partners. Participate in admissions planning meetings, territory reviews, and strategic enrollment initiatives. Contribute to a collaborative, innovative team focused on student success and continuous improvement. What We're Looking For Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong organizational, planning, and time management abilities. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrated ability to build authentic relationships with diverse populations. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and the ability to quickly learn CRM and enrollment technologies. Valid driver's license and ability to travel extensively, including evenings and weekends. Preferred Qualifications Experience in undergraduate admissions, enrollment management, or higher education recruitment. Experience using CRM platforms such as Slate, Salesforce, TargetX, or similar systems. Experience analyzing enrollment data and performance metrics. Presentation or public speaking experience. Bilingual or multilingual communication skills. Success in This Role The ideal candidate is: Passionate about helping students achieve their educational goals. An exceptional relationship builder who creates trust and lasting connections. Strategic, analytical, and comfortable making data-informed decisions. Highly organized with excellent follow-through. Adaptable and energized by a fast-paced, goal-oriented environment. A collaborative team player who enjoys partnering across campus. Professional, accountable, and committed to delivering outstanding student experience. Physical Requirements & Travel This position requires frequent travel throughout an assigned recruitment territory, including visits to high schools, college fairs, community organizations, and recruitment events. Evening and weekend work is required throughout the recruitment cycle to support admissions programming and enrollment initiatives. Compensation & Benefits Salary Range: $40,000-$50,000 annually Actual compensation will be commensurate with education, experience, skills, internal equity, and market considerations. Benefits Highlights Maryville University offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support the health, financial well-being, and professional growth of our employees. Eligible employees enjoy access to: Medical, dental, and vision coverage Retirement plan with 100% University matching up to 9% contributions University-paid life and long-term disability insurance Generous paid time off, including 18 holidays, 3 weeks of vacation, 12 sick days, and 4 personal days Full/Partial Tuition waived for employees and eligible dependents Hybrid and flexible work schedules Wellness programs and employee assistance resources Free parking, fitness center access, and other campus perks"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001215023006": {
      "title": "Bascom Honors Directorship",
      "description": "Bascom Honors Directorship. Director of the Bascom Honors Program Position summary Maryville University invites applications for the Director of the Bascom Honors Program. The Director leads Bascom Honors and works closely with faculty, students, and academic and enrollment partners across the university to carry the program’s legacy forward and shape a program that stands apart from conventional honors models. Responsibilities › Lead and grow the Bascom Honors Program, including its curriculum, signature experiences, and student community. Develop a service-learning component as part of the Bascom Honors Program. This will include organizing pedagogy and curriculum around identified learning outcomes. It is anticipated that all Honors students will participate in designated service learning courses/experiences. › Articulate and pursue a vision for honors education that is distinctive by design, using experiential and interdisciplinary approaches that set the program apart. › Connect the program to Maryville’s broader academic mission and student achievement framework. › Advise and mentor honors students and support their pursuit of research, fellowships, and graduate study. › Partner with enrollment colleagues on recruitment, access, and student success. › Steward the program’s partnerships, including international and study abroad opportunities. › Partner with advancement on fundraising, donor stewardship, and growth of program resources. › Represent the program to internal and external audiences. Required qualifications › An earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree. › A minimum of 10 years of faculty experience. › A compelling vision for an honors program that is distinct from typical models. › A record of teaching excellence, student mentorship, and academic leadership. Preferred qualifications › Experience developing distinctive, interdisciplinary, or experiential academic programs. › A commitment to the liberal arts and to authentic, rigorous learning. › Experience building community-engaged learning or partnerships with external organizations. › A record of fostering inclusive, globally minded learning communities; international scholarship or study experience. › Experience developing research agendas or securing external funding."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001205208406": {
      "title": "Director, Physical Therapy Program",
      "description": "Director, Physical Therapy Program. Program Director of Physical Therapy Program Full-Time Faculty Leadership Position Lead the Future of Physical Therapy Education At Maryville University, we power dreams—not just degrees. As an innovative leader in higher education, Maryville University is committed to preparing healthcare professionals who are ready to transform lives and strengthen communities. The Walker College of Health Professions invites applications for the Program Director of the Physical Therapy Program. We seek an accomplished educator, leader, and clinician-scholar who is passionate about advancing physical therapy education, supporting faculty excellence, and fostering student success. This leadership position offers the opportunity to shape the strategic direction of a growing program while ensuring academic excellence, compliance with accreditation standards, and exceptional student outcomes. What You'll Do Academic & Curriculum Leadership Provide strategic leadership for the Physical Therapy Program. Lead the ongoing review, development, and continuous improvement of curriculum. Ensure curriculum aligns with accreditation requirements, industry trends, and best practices in physical therapy education. Guide curriculum proposals through university governance processes and maintain accurate program documentation. Collaborate with college leadership to support long-term academic planning and program growth. Program Planning & Assessment Lead program assessment efforts and utilize outcomes data to drive continuous improvement. Monitor student achievement, licensure outcomes, and program effectiveness metrics. Develop and implement strategies that support student success and program excellence. Accreditation & Compliance Serve as the primary liaison to accreditation agencies and regulatory bodies. Ensure ongoing compliance with all accreditation standards and reporting requirements. Lead accreditation self-studies, site visit preparation, annual reporting, and program review activities. Faculty Leadership & Development Recruit, hire, onboard, mentor, and evaluate full-time and adjunct faculty. Foster a culture of collaboration, innovation, and continuous professional growth. Provide leadership in faculty development, performance management, and succession planning. Support teaching excellence through observation, coaching, and ongoing feedback. Student Recruitment, Retention & Success Provide leadership for student recruitment and retention initiatives. Participate in admissions-related activities and recruitment events. Serve as the primary point of contact for program-level academic and professional conduct matters. Oversee recommendations regarding admissions, progression, graduation, and academic standing. Program Operations & Resource Management Oversee course scheduling, faculty assignments, and instructional resources. Develop annual budget requests and manage program resources effectively. Collaborate with university partners to identify grants, donations, contracts, and other external funding opportunities. Ensure operational decisions support program priorities and institutional goals. Internal & External Engagement Build and maintain relationships with healthcare organizations, clinical partners, professional associations, and alumni. Collaborate across the Walker College of Health Professions and the broader university community. Represent the program within professional organizations and the physical therapy profession. Serve on college and university committees as assigned. What We're Looking For Required Qualifications An academic doctorate degree from a regionally accredited institution. Minimum of six years of teaching experience in higher education. Minimum of three years of full-time experience as core faculty in a CAPTE-accredited entry-level physical therapist education program. Demonstrated experience in academic leadership, curriculum development, and program administration. Knowledge of current issues, trends, and accreditation standards within physical therapy education. Ability to teach within the Physical Therapy curriculum and area of expertise. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience serving as a Program Director, Associate Program Director, Department Chair, or similar academic leadership role. Experience leading accreditation activities, self-studies, and site visits. Experience managing budgets, personnel, and strategic initiatives. Established professional network within the physical therapy profession. Record of scholarship, service, and professional engagement. Key Competencies Strategic leadership and decision-making Faculty mentoring and development Accreditation and regulatory compliance Curriculum design and assessment Budget and resource management Relationship building and collaboration Strong written and verbal communication skills Why Maryville? Maryville University is recognized for innovation, student-centered learning, and a commitment to preparing graduates who make meaningful contributions to their professions and communities. As Program Director, you will have the opportunity to influence the next generation of physical therapists while shaping the future of an established and respected academic program. Join a university community dedicated to helping students learn deeply, serve boldly, and lead with heart. Compensation & Benefits Salary Range: $100,000-120,000 annually Actual compensation will be commensurate with education, experience, skills, internal equity, and market considerations. Benefits Highlights Maryville University offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support the health, financial well-being, and professional growth of our employees. Eligible employees enjoy access to: Medical, dental, and vision coverage Retirement plan with 100% University matching up to 9% contributions University-paid life and long-term disability insurance Generous paid time off, including 18 holidays, 3 weeks of vacation, 12 sick days, and 4 personal days Full/Partial Tuition waived for employees and eligible dependents Hybrid and flexible work schedules Wellness programs and employee assistance resources Free parking, fitness center access, and other campus perks"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001197335006": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Pediatric Primary Care NP Program",
      "description": "Coordinator, Pediatric Primary Care NP Program. Maryville University is seeking a Coordinator for the Pediatric Primary Care Nurse Practitioner (PNP) Concentration. This role is ideal for an experienced Pediatric Nurse Practitioner and educator who is passionate about supporting faculty and student success and advancing innovative, high-quality nursing education. The Coordinator will play a key role in program growth, clinical partnership development, curriculum excellence, and fostering an inclusive learning environment aligned with the University's mission and values. Key Responsibilities 1. Oversee the PNP Nurse Practitioner concentration. Additional duties as assigned to meet program needs. 2. Oversee and support students with preceptor placements, clinical site communication as needed, and supporting paperwork. Academic advising and mentoring as needed. 3. Oversee, credential, and manage faculty in the PNP concentration to support excellent curriculum delivery to ensure that educational objectives of the program are attained and aligned for preparation for certification exams. 4. Develop and guide strategic plans for program growth and goals in alignment with the Catherine McCauley School of Nursing, Walker College of Health Professions, and Maryville University’s mission, vision, and values. 5. Maintain relationships with internal and external constituencies, including educational partners, students, serve on committees, and represent the university at external functions as required. Including attending meetings as required. 6. Remain committed to fostering a culturally diverse and inclusive atmosphere for faculty, staff, and students. Teaching as required per contract Qualifications Required Knowledge Current Pediatric Nurse Practitioner clinical practice knowledge. Preferred knowledge of preceptorships for Pediatric Nurse Practitioner Students. Knowledge of online learning management system(s). Knowledge of how to support students and faculty in achieving academic goals and outcomes. Required Skills/Abilities Prior online teaching experience. Preferred prior online teaching experience as an NP/PNP. Highly detail-oriented and analytical. Mentally nimble to balance multiple competing priorities. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with short deadlines. Experience and comfortable with technology, databases, MS Office, and the ability to learn other software systems. Sales Force experience is a plus. Prior leadership and/or mentoring experience preferred. Ability to remain calm, provide leadership, and use emotional intelligence in difficult conversations. Formal Education MSN, nationally certified as a Nurse Practitioner (Pediatric Primary Care), with a minimum of five years of recent clinical experience as an NP/PNP, and unencumbered RN licensure in the United States. Preferred Doctorate in Nursing or related field. Preferred NP clinical experience patient populations."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001140622206": {
      "title": "Biology Adjunct",
      "description": "Biology Adjunct. The College of Arts, Sciences and Education is accepting applications for an adjunct instructor to teach in-person introductory Anatomy and Physiology laboratory sections. Must be available between 8 am and 6 pm from January 11, 2027 - May 2, 2027. Candidates should have a minimum of Master’s degree in Biology or a commensurate degree in the health professions. The successful candidate will facilitate hands-on laboratory activities that support student understanding of human anatomy and physiology. Prior teaching experience is preferred. Candidates should have a minimum of Master’s degree in Biology or a commensurate degree in the health professions. The successful candidate will facilitate hands-on laboratory activities that support student understanding of human anatomy and physiology. Prior teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001233606206": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Public Safety Officer. Public Safety Officer Shift: Overnight (10:00 PM-6:00 AM) At Maryville University, we power dreams—not just degrees. Our mission extends beyond the classroom. We are committed to creating a safe, welcoming, and supportive environment where students, faculty, staff, and visitors can learn, work, and thrive. Maryville University is seeking a dedicated and service-oriented Public Safety Officer to join our campus safety team. This role is ideal for individuals who are passionate about public service, community engagement, emergency response, and helping others. Public Safety Officers play a critical role in maintaining a secure campus environment by conducting proactive patrols, responding to emergencies, assisting the community, and enforcing university policies and applicable laws. What You'll Do Campus Safety & Security Conduct proactive foot and vehicle patrols across campus to maintain a safe and secure environment. Monitor campus facilities and grounds, identify safety concerns, and ensure building security. Respond to security alarms, fire alarms, suspicious activity, and calls for service. Detect and deter criminal activity and take appropriate enforcement action when necessary. Emergency Response Respond promptly to medical emergencies and provide first aid, CPR, and AED assistance when needed. Assist during campus emergencies, severe weather events, evacuations, and other crisis situations. Support emergency preparedness efforts and help ensure the safety of the university community. Investigations & Reporting Conduct preliminary investigations and gather information related to incidents and criminal activity. Maintain accurate reports, daily logs, and incident documentation. Assist with follow-up investigations as directed. Community Engagement & Service Provide assistance to students, employees, and visitors. Enforce university parking regulations and assist motorists as needed. Direct traffic during special events and emergencies. Foster positive relationships through professionalism, visibility, and customer service. Professional Development Participate in required training programs, including: First Aid/CPR/AED Firearms certification OC Spray and Baton certification Active Shooter Response De-escalation techniques Other department-required training What We're Looking For Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Ability to obtain and maintain: Metro Security License Firearms certification OC Spray certification ASP Baton certification Handcuff certification First Aid, CPR, and AED certification Knowledge & Skills Knowledge of local, state, and federal laws and regulations. Understanding of security and law enforcement practices, preferably within a higher education environment. Strong communication, interpersonal, and conflict-resolution skills. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Strong organizational and report-writing skills. Commitment to professionalism, integrity, and service. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with and serve a diverse campus community. Preferred Qualifications Prior law enforcement, military, campus safety, security, or emergency response experience. Experience working in a higher education environment. Familiarity with security technologies such as CCTV, access control systems, and ID card systems. Working Environment Public Safety Officers serve in a dynamic environment and must be prepared to respond to a wide range of situations, including: Medical emergencies Fire and life-safety incidents Severe weather events Hazardous materials incidents Campus emergencies and critical incidents Additional requirements include: Ability to stand and walk for extended periods Ability to lift, push, pull, or carry up to 45 pounds Ability to perform foot patrols and operate a patrol vehicle Ability to provide CPR and first aid without assistance Availability to work evenings, overnight shifts, weekends, holidays, and other assigned schedules Exceptional Time-Off Benefits Because Public Safety Officers provide critical campus coverage during periods when many university offices are closed, Maryville offers paid Replacement Holidays in addition to vacation and sick leave. Replacement Holidays are provided to recognize coverage requirements during university-observed holidays and breaks, helping ensure officers receive equitable paid time off comparable to that of other university employees. Why Maryville? At Maryville University, our people matter most. We believe in fostering a culture where employees are empowered to make a meaningful impact every day. As a Public Safety Officer, you'll play an essential role in protecting our community while supporting student success and well-being. Join a team that helps students learn deeply, serve boldly, and lead with heart."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/facultyandstaffmaryvilleuniversityexternalcs/cx/job-details?reqId=5001189665006": {
      "title": "Accounting - Adjunct",
      "description": "Accounting - Adjunct. The College of Business and Technology is accepting applications for academically or professionally qualified adjunct faculty members to teach in-person undergraduate Accounting courses. Including: FINANCIAL ACCOUNTING Tuesday Thursday 12:30-1:45 1/11/2027 - 5/2/2027 Course Descriptions Three-credit-hour courses designed to deepen students' understanding of accounting concepts. Students will learn to acquire, analyze, and critically evaluate both financial and non-financial information to make effective business decisions, taking into account strategic, technological, and environmental considerations. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities: Teach assigned course as specified in the schedule and course contract. Participate in welcome orientation to become familiar with the University’s mission, academic policies and procedures, expectations, and Canvas (Learning Management System). Prepare essential learning objectives, lesson plans, and assignments. Develop course syllabus. Clearly communicate course objectives and learning outcomes, teaching methodology, and assignments and deadlines. Employ a variety of teaching styles in order to effectively deliver course content demonstrating both academic and real-world applications of concepts covered. Encourage active learning through discussion topics, class assignments, group projects, etc. Provide feedback and grade assignments in a timely and thorough manner (with 24-36 hrs.). Establish digital office hours to provide additional assistance with student questions/concerns. Report early alerts for students who are not actively engaging in the course. Additional duties as assigned Qualifications Minimum Qualification: Master’s degree in Accounting or a related field Preferred Qualification: PhD in Accounting or a related field"
    }
  },
